 # Voxel Texture Atlas
 
-Also called: Runtime Voxel Texture Atlas, OpenTESArena Voxel Atlas
 
 ## Overview
-A technique to combine multiple discrete voxel textures into a single large 2D texture (atlas) at runtime to reduce CPU-bound performance overhead caused by frequent material binding calls during rendering [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the inefficiency of legacy systems where voxel data is organized as multiple separate textures per entity (e.g., 3–4 textures per building in .SET files) by sub-allocating them within one unified texture object [S1, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that may focus on static packing or 3D volume atlases, this method specifically targets runtime dynamic allocation for voxel-based geometry to optimize draw call batching in CPU-limited scenarios [S1, unofficial].
+A technique to combine multiple discrete voxel textures into a single large 2D texture (atlas) at runtime to reduce CPU-bound performance overhead caused by frequent material binding calls during rendering [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the inefficiency of legacy systems where voxel data is organized as multiple separate textures per entity (e.g., 3–4 textures per building in `.SET` files) by sub-allocating them within one unified texture object [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Texture Uniting (Multi-Channel Packing)](2470-texture-uniting-multi-channel-packing.md) or [3D Volume Atlas Packing](7158-3d-volume-atlas-packing.md), this method specifically targets runtime dynamic allocation for voxel-based geometry to optimize draw call batching in CPU-limited scenarios [S1, unofficial].
 
